  "status": "PROVED REFINEMENT: quartic affine-line factors are centered powers",
  "task": "X39 h=4 affine-line normal form",
  "theorem": "Let psi be a monic quartic over characteristic p>4.  If psi(aX+b)=psi(X) for a nonidentity affine map, then translations a=1,b!=0 are impossible.  For a!=1, with c=b/(1-a), the shifted polynomial psi(T+c) is invariant under T -> aT.  The leading term forces a^4=1, so ord(a) is 2 or 4, and all nonzero shifted exponents are multiples of ord(a).  Hence psi=Phi((X-c)^m), m in {2,4}.  The c=0 branch is cyclic-paid; the c!=0 branch is the named centered-power affine residue.",
